/*Q1. Develop a text-processing application using a Java interface and two implementation classes to retrieve the first and last characters of a
string.
Interface: GetCharacter
Create an interface named GetCharacter that declares the following method:
• void displayChar(String inputString, int position) — retrieves and displays a character from the given string.
Class 1: FirstCharacter
Create a class named FirstCharacter that implements the GetCharacter interface.
Override displayChar() with the following behavior:
• Retrieve and display the first character of the input string in the below format:
First Character:
Class 2: LastCharacter
Create a class named LastCharacter that implements the GetCharacter interface.
Override displayChar() with the following behavior:
• Retrieve and display the last character of the input string in the below format:
Last Character:
The position parameter is part of the required method signature but is not used by either implementation.
The TextProcessing class should read a string, create objects of FirstCharacter and LastCharacter using GetCharacter references, and invoke
displayChar() on both objects.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a non-empty string.
• The string may contain letters, digits, spaces, and punctuation marks.
• Standard Java char characters are supported. Unicode characters represented by a single UTF-16 code unit can be processed;
supplementary Unicode characters represented by surrogate pairs are not treated as a single character.
Output Format:
• Display the first character on the first line, in the below format:
First Character:
• Display the last character on the second line, in the below format:
Last Character:
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
interface GetCharacter {
    void displayChar(String inputString, int position);
}
 
class FirstCharacter implements GetCharacter {
    @Override
    public void displayChar(String inputString, int position) {
        System.out.println("First Character: " + inputString.charAt(0));
    }
}
 
class LastCharacter implements GetCharacter {
    @Override
    public void displayChar(String inputString, int position) {
        int last = inputString.length() - 1;
        System.out.println("Last Character: " + inputString.charAt(last));
    }
}
 
public class TextProcessing {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        GetCharacter first = new FirstCharacter();   // interface reference
        GetCharacter last = new LastCharacter();
        first.displayChar(s, 0);
        last.displayChar(s, s.length() - 1);
        sc.close();
    }
}
